<h2>Your options</h2>
<ul class="checklist">
  <li><strong>In-office whitening.</strong> A single appointment, supervised, with the strongest professional-grade gel. Results visible immediately.</li>
  <li><strong>Custom take-home trays.</strong> We make trays molded to your teeth, you whiten at home over 1–2 weeks. The trays last for years of touch-ups.</li>
  <li><strong>Combination.</strong> A jump-start in-office plus take-home trays for maintenance — popular for events or weddings.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Before you whiten</h2>
<p>Whitening works best on natural tooth structure. Crowns, veneers, and tooth-colored fillings don't change color. If you have visible restorations in your smile, we'll plan around them so the final result looks even. A cleaning before whitening also helps the gel reach the enamel evenly.</p>

<h2>Why professional whitening beats store-bought strips</h2>
<p>Over-the-counter strips and toothpastes use low-strength gel and one-size trays, so the gel slides around, misses the edges of your teeth and can irritate your gums. Professional whitening uses stronger gel in trays shaped to your teeth, with your gums protected. That means a more even result in less time, and less guesswork about what's safe.</p>

<h2>Who is a good candidate</h2>
<ul class="checklist">
  <li>Yellowing from coffee, tea, red wine or aging usually responds very well</li>
  <li>Brown or gray staining from medication, fluorosis or an old injury is more stubborn, and veneers or bonding may give a better result</li>
  <li>Teeth and gums should be healthy first, so we treat cavities and gum inflammation before whitening</li>
  <li>Whitening isn't recommended during pregnancy or while nursing</li>
</ul>

<h2>Keeping your results</h2>
<p>Rinse with water after coffee, tea or red wine, keep up with cleanings every six months, and use your custom trays for a short touch-up when you notice your shade slipping. Most patients touch up once or twice a year.</p>

<h2>Whitening as part of a bigger smile plan</h2>
<p>Whitening is often the first step in a cosmetic plan because it sets the shade that any new <a href="/services/veneers/">veneers</a>, bonding or <a href="/services/crowns-bridges/">crowns</a> are matched to. If you're thinking about more than whitening, see our <a href="/services/cosmetic-dentistry/">cosmetic dentistry</a> page or ask Dr. Phillips at a cosmetic consultation in our Tempe office.</p>
